1. Introduction & Overview

CIP2 is a macOS-focused (Apple Silicon optimized) Electron application providing a specialized visual interface for managing JSON data structured around Fields of Interest (FoIs) and their associated Programs. It replaces manual JSON editing with interactive, dynamic, force-directed graph visualizations and inline editing capabilities. CIP2 reads from and writes to a user-specified JSON file, employing a "last save wins" strategy for shared file scenarios. The aesthetic goal is "light academia minimalism".

2. Goals

Provide an intuitive, visual workflow for navigating hierarchical FoI/Program data.
Enable efficient, inline editing of Program details and their categorization under FoIs.
Persist inclusion/exclusion status for both FoIs and Programs within the JSON data.
Ensure data integrity via explicit and triggered save actions with clear user feedback.
Deliver a fluid, engaging, and aesthetically pleasing user experience through smooth animations and dynamic layouts.
Support team collaboration on a shared JSON file ("last save wins").
Maintain forward compatibility by gracefully handling unknown fields in the JSON schema.
3. Target Audience & Platform

Users: Internal team members maintaining the FoI/Program dataset.
Platform: macOS (Optimized builds for Apple Silicon - M1 or later). Assumed standard macOS UI conventions where applicable.
Rollout: Initial limited internal release.
4. Data Model & Handling

4.1. JSON Structure

CIP2 operates on a JSON file structured as a single top-level object. Keys of this object are the Field of Interest names (strings), and values are FoI objects.

{
  "Mathematics": {                     // Key: String, the unique name/identifier for the FoI.
    "included": true,                  // Boolean: FoI inclusion status. Required.
    "population": {                    // Object: Aggregate data. Required for display logic.
      "count": 132065,                 // Integer: Population/interest metric. Required.
      "as_of": "2025-04-25"            // String: ISO-8601 date (YYYY-MM-DD). Required.
    },
    "programs": [                      // Array: List of programs. MUST be present. Can be empty.
      {
        "name": "Algebra Club",        // String: Official program title. Required.
        "degree": "BS",                // String: Credential type. Can be empty/null.
        "description": "...",          // String: Blurb. Can be empty/null.
        "link": "https://...",         // String: Canonical URL. Required. Must be valid URL format.
        "included": true               // Boolean: Program inclusion status. Required.
        // CIP2 must ignore any additional unknown fields here
      }
      // ... additional programs ...
    ]
    // CIP2 must ignore any additional unknown fields here (e.g., notes, internal_id)
  },
  "Computer Science": {
    "included": true,
    "population": { /* ... */ },
    "programs": [ /* ... */ ]
  }
  // ... additional FoIs (keys are the FoI names) ...
}
